---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-stack</code> lays its children out in a column, or in a row with
  <code>direction="horizontal"</code>. The element itself is the flex container, so the children
  are its flex items with nothing in between. <code>gap</code> takes a step of the spacing scale:
  <code>gap="200"</code> is <code>var(--spacing-200)</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-stack gap='200' style='width: 100%; max-width: 320px;'>
    <wc-card variant='outlined'><wc-card-content>First item</wc-card-content></wc-card>
    <wc-card variant='outlined'><wc-card-content>Second item</wc-card-content></wc-card>
    <wc-card variant='outlined'><wc-card-content>Third item</wc-card-content></wc-card>
  </wc-stack>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Rows</h3>
<p>
  A horizontal stack follows the writing direction, so it runs right to left in RTL.
  <code>align</code> sets <code>align-items</code> (<code>start</code>, <code>center</code>,
  <code>end</code>, <code>stretch</code>, <code>baseline</code>) and <code>justify</code> sets
  <code>justify-content</code> (<code>start</code>, <code>center</code>, <code>end</code>,
  <code>space-between</code>, <code>space-around</code>, <code>space-evenly</code>).
  <code>wrap</code> lets the items wrap.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-stack direction='horizontal' gap='100' align='center' justify='space-between' style='width: 100%;'>
    <wc-avatar name='Ada Lovelace'></wc-avatar>
    <span>Ada Lovelace</span>
    <wc-button>Follow</wc-button>
  </wc-stack>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Spacing steps</h3>
<p>
  The steps are <code>000</code>, <code>025</code>, <code>050</code>, <code>075</code>,
  <code>100</code>, <code>150</code>, <code>200</code>, <code>250</code>, <code>300</code>,
  <code>400</code>, <code>500</code>, <code>600</code>, <code>800</code>, <code>1000</code>,
  <code>1200</code> and <code>2000</code>. Without <code>gap</code> there is none; a
  <code>style="gap: …"</code> on the element still wins.
</p>
